IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`

-- coa12-ch3b-rights.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 16, Chapter 3: "Duties and rights of auditors" from s 499, "Signature of
-- auditor's report" and "Offences in connection with auditor's report": ss 499, 500, 501, 502, 503, 504, 505, 506, 507, 508, 509
-- (lines 7050-7168 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively. See coa12-ch3a-report.l4 for how to read an answer.
-- Forks F1-F9 are in NOTES.md. Keel and other-part answers are INPUTS named as PLAN.md 4.1 and 4.2 name them.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 499  Auditor's general right to information
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 499(1)(a)
-- Plain gloss: an auditor may see the company's books, accounts and vouchers at any time, in whatever form they are held.
-- src:7051 | (1) An auditor of a company—
-- src:7052 | (a) has a right of access at all times to the company's books, accounts and vouchers (in whatever form they are held), and
@ref s 499(1)(a) Right of access at all times (src:7051-7052)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is one of the company's books, accounts or vouchers (in whatever form they are held)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 499(1)(a) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor of the company` AND `the item is one of the company's books, accounts or vouchers (in whatever form they are held)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a company— (a) has a right of access at all times to the company's books, accounts and vouchers (in whatever form they are held)"

-- COVERS: s 499(2), s 499(2)(a), s 499(2)(b), s 499(2)(c), s 499(2)(d), s 499(2)(e)
-- Plain gloss: the people an auditor may require to give information: officers and employees; whoever holds the books; UK-incorporated subsidiary undertakings; their officers, employees, auditors and book-holders; and anyone who was one of those at a time the information is about.
-- src:7054 | (2) Those persons are—
-- src:7055 | (a) any officer or employee of the company;
-- src:7056 | (b) any person holding or accountable for any of the company's books, accounts or vouchers;
-- src:7057 | (c) any subsidiary undertaking of the company which is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom;
-- src:7058 | (d) any officer, employee or auditor of any such subsidiary undertaking or any person holding or accountable for any books, accounts or vouchers of any such subsidiary undertaking;
-- src:7059 | (e) any person who fell within any of paragraphs (a) to (d) at a time to which the information or explanations required by the auditor relates or relate.
@ref s 499(2) The persons the auditor may require (src:7054-7059)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds or is accountable for any of the company's books, accounts or vouchers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subsidiary undertaking of the company which is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer, employee or auditor of such a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds or is accountable for any books, accounts or vouchers of such a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fell within any of paragraphs (a) to (d) at a time to which the information or explanations required by the auditor relate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 499(2) the person is one the auditor may require to provide information or explanations` MEANS
    IF       `the person is an officer or employee of the company`
          OR `the person holds or is accountable for any of the company's books, accounts or vouchers`
          OR `the person is a subsidiary undertaking of the company which is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom`
          OR `the person is an officer, employee or auditor of such a subsidiary undertaking`
          OR `the person holds or is accountable for any books, accounts or vouchers of such a subsidiary undertaking`
          OR `the person fell within any of paragraphs (a) to (d) at a time to which the information or explanations required by the auditor relate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those persons are— (a) any officer or employee of the company; ... (e) any person who fell within any of paragraphs (a) to (d) ..." (a list under "are", read as closed: fork F3)

-- COVERS: s 499(1)(b), s 499(1)
-- Plain gloss: an auditor may require any of those people to give him the information or explanations he thinks he needs to do his job.
-- src:7053 | (b) may require any of the following persons to provide him with such information or explanations as he thinks necessary for the performance of his duties as auditor.
@ref s 499(1)(b) Power to require information or explanations (src:7053-7053)
GIVEN `the person requiring is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 499(2) the person is one the auditor may require` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor thinks the information or explanations necessary for the performance of his duties as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 499(1)(b) the auditor may require the person to provide the information or explanations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 499(2) the person is one the auditor may require` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may require any of the following persons"; the person is none of them (see s 499(2)); the grant is to require "any of the following persons" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose list gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        IF (NOT `the person requiring is an auditor of the company`) OR (NOT `the auditor thinks the information or explanations necessary for the performance of his duties as auditor`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a company— ... may require ... such information or explanations as he thinks necessary for the performance of his duties as auditor"
        OTHERWISE `s 499(2) the person is one the auditor may require` -- JUST TRUE, or NOTHING where s 499(2) is not known

-- COVERS: s 499(3)
-- Plain gloss: what a person says in answer to an auditor's requirement cannot be used against him in a criminal case, except a prosecution under s 501.
-- src:7060 | (3) A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under this section may not be used in evidence against him in criminal proceedings except proceedings for an offence under section 501.
@ref s 499(3) Use of the statement in evidence (src:7060-7060)
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement under section 499` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an offence under section 501` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 499(3) the statement may be used in evidence against the person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the statement was made in response to a requirement under section 499`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under this section"
    ELSE IF `the proceedings are criminal proceedings` AND (NOT `the proceedings are for an offence under section 501`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be used in evidence against him in criminal proceedings except proceedings for an offence under section 501"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "in criminal proceedings" and lifts for "proceedings for an offence under section 501"; the subsection does not say the statement may then be used, nor speak of other proceedings (fork F6: an "except" once met)

-- COVERS: s 499(4)
-- Plain gloss: the section never forces anyone to hand over what legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications) protects.
-- src:7061 | (4) Nothing in this section compels a person to disclose information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings.
@ref s 499(4) Legal professional privilege (src:7061-7061)
GIVEN `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 499(4) the section compels the person to disclose the information` MEANS
    IF `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section compels a person to disclose information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege ... could be maintained in legal proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection only says what the section does not compel; for other information it does not say that the section compels disclosure

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 500  Auditor's right to information from overseas subsidiaries
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 500(1)
-- Plain gloss: where a parent company has a subsidiary undertaking outside the UK, the parent's auditor may require the parent to get the information or explanations he reasonably needs from that undertaking and the people listed in (2).
-- src:7063 | (1) Where a parent company has a subsidiary undertaking that is not a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom, the auditor of the parent company may require it to obtain from any of the following persons such information or explanations as he may reasonably require for the purposes of his duties as auditor.
@ref s 500(1) Power to require information from an overseas subsidiary (src:7063-7063)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary undertaking is not a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requiring is the auditor of the parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor reasonably requires the information or explanations for the purposes of his duties as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(1) the auditor of the parent company may require it to obtain information or explanations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a parent company has a subsidiary undertaking" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a parent company is section 1173(1) (keel), not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the subsidiary undertaking is not a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a subsidiary undertaking that is not a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")
        ELSE IF `the person requiring is the auditor of the parent company` AND `the auditor reasonably requires the information or explanations for the purposes of his duties as auditor`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the auditor of the parent company may require it to obtain ... such information or explanations as he may reasonably require for the purposes of his duties as auditor"

-- COVERS: s 500(2), s 500(2)(a), s 500(2)(b), s 500(2)(c), s 500(2)(d)
-- Plain gloss: the people the overseas undertaking may be required to obtain information from: itself; its officers, employees and auditor; whoever holds its books; and anyone who was one of those at a time the information is about.
-- src:7064 | (2) Those persons are—
-- src:7065 | (a) the undertaking;
-- src:7066 | (b) any officer, employee or auditor of the undertaking;
-- src:7067 | (c) any person holding or accountable for any of the undertaking's books, accounts or vouchers;
-- src:7068 | (d) any person who fell within paragraph (b) or (c) at a time to which the information or explanations relates or relate.
@ref s 500(2) The persons from whom information may be obtained (src:7064-7068)
GIVEN `the person is the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer, employee or auditor of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds or is accountable for any of the undertaking's books, accounts or vouchers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fell within paragraph (b) or (c) at a time to which the information or explanations relate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(2) the person is one from whom the undertaking may be required to obtain information` MEANS
    IF       `the person is the undertaking`
          OR `the person is an officer, employee or auditor of the undertaking`
          OR `the person holds or is accountable for any of the undertaking's books, accounts or vouchers`
          OR `the person fell within paragraph (b) or (c) at a time to which the information or explanations relate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those persons are— (a) the undertaking; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ..." (a list under "are", read as closed: fork F3)

-- COVERS: s 500(3)
-- Plain gloss: if the auditor so requires, the parent company must take all the steps reasonably open to it to get the information.
-- src:7069 | (3) If so required, the parent company must take all such steps as are reasonably open to it to obtain the information or explanations from the person concerned.
@ref s 500(3) The parent company's duty to take steps (src:7069-7069)
GIVEN `the auditor has so required under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(3) the parent company must take all such steps as are reasonably open to it to obtain the information or explanations` MEANS
    IF `the auditor has so required under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If so required, the parent company must take all such steps" (fork F1: a duty whose "if" is unmet)

-- The same duty as a deontic rule. No period is stated, so there is no WITHIN.
@ref s 500(3) The parent company's duty to take steps (src:7069-7069)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 500(3) the parent company's duty to take steps to obtain the information` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Auditor, "take all such steps as are reasonably open to it to obtain the information or explanations from the person concerned"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- COVERS: s 500(4)
-- Plain gloss: as s 499(3), for what a person says in answer to a requirement under s 500.
-- src:7070 | (4) A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under this section may not be used in evidence against him in criminal proceedings except proceedings for an offence under section 501.
@ref s 500(4) Use of the statement in evidence (src:7070-7070)
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement under section 500` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an offence under section 501` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(4) the statement may be used in evidence against the person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the statement was made in response to a requirement under section 500`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under this section"
    ELSE IF `the proceedings are criminal proceedings` AND (NOT `the proceedings are for an offence under section 501`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be used in evidence against him in criminal proceedings except proceedings for an offence under section 501"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "in criminal proceedings" and lifts for "proceedings for an offence under section 501"; the subsection does not say the statement may then be used (fork F6)

-- COVERS: s 500(5)
-- Plain gloss: as s 499(4).
-- src:7071 | (5) Nothing in this section compels a person to disclose information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings.
@ref s 500(5) Legal professional privilege (src:7071-7071)
GIVEN `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(5) the section compels the person to disclose the information` MEANS
    IF `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section compels a person to disclose information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege ... could be maintained in legal proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection only says what the section does not compel

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 501  Auditor's rights to information: offences
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 501(1), s 501(1)(a), s 501(1)(b)
-- Plain gloss: it is an offence to give an auditor, knowingly or recklessly, a statement that purports to give information he requires or may require under s 499 and is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
-- src:7073 | (1) A person commits an offence who knowingly or recklessly makes to an auditor of a company a statement (oral or written) that—
-- src:7074 | (a) conveys or purports to convey any information or explanations which the auditor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 499, and
-- src:7075 | (b) is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 501(1) Misleading statements to an auditor (src:7073-7075)
GIVEN `the person makes to an auditor of a company a statement (oral or written)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement conveys or purports to convey any information or explanations which the auditor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 499` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(1) the person commits an offence by a misleading statement to an auditor` MEANS
    IF       `the person makes to an auditor of a company a statement (oral or written)`
         AND `the person does so knowingly or recklessly`
         AND `the statement conveys or purports to convey any information or explanations which the auditor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 499`
         AND `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence who knowingly or recklessly makes to an auditor of a company a statement ... that— (a) conveys or purports to convey ..., and (b) is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular" (an offence defined by "who", read as closed: this section gives no offence on these facts; marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 501(2), s 501(2)(a), s 501(2)(b), s 501(2)(b)(i), s 501(2)(b)(ii)
-- Plain gloss: the most the court can impose for the s 501(1) offence: on indictment two years or a fine or both; summary, twelve months (England and Wales) or six months (Scotland, Northern Ireland), or a fine up to the statutory maximum, or both.
-- src:7076 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable—
-- src:7077 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:7078 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:7079 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:7080 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 501(2) The penalty for the offence in subsection (1) (src:7076-7080)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 501(2) the penalty for an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text sets different maxima for England and Wales and for Scotland or Northern Ireland and does not say which applies to a summary conviction with no place named

-- COVERS: s 501(3)
-- Plain gloss: it is an offence to fail to comply, without delay, with an auditor's requirement under s 499, unless it was not reasonably practicable to provide the information.
-- src:7081 | (3) A person who fails to comply with a requirement under section 499 without delay commits an offence unless it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanations.
@ref s 501(3) Failure to comply with a requirement without delay (src:7081-7081)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement under section 499 without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(3) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with a requirement under section 499` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person fails to comply with a requirement under section 499 without delay`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who fails to comply with a requirement under section 499 without delay commits an offence" (the person did not fail)
    ELSE IF `it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanations`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanations" (fork F6: an "unless" once met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 501(4), s 501(4)(a)
-- Plain gloss: if a parent company fails to comply with s 500, the company commits the offence.
-- src:7082 | (4) If a parent company fails to comply with section 500, an offence is committed by—
-- src:7083 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 501(4)(a) The parent company (src:7082-7083)
GIVEN `the parent company fails to comply with section 500` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(4)(a) the parent company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the parent company fails to comply with section 500`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a parent company fails to comply with section 500, an offence is committed by— (a) the company" (marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 501(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: and by every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:7082 | (4) If a parent company fails to comply with section 500, an offence is committed by—
-- src:7084 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 501(4)(b) Officers in default (src:7082-7084)
GIVEN `the parent company fails to comply with section 500` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(4)(b) the officer of the parent company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the parent company fails to comply with section 500`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (the officer is not in default: section 1121), or NOTHING where section 1121 is not known
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a parent company fails to comply with section 500, an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 501(5)
-- Plain gloss: the penalty for the s 501(3) and (4) offences: on summary conviction, a fine up to level 3 on the standard scale.
-- src:7085 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) or (4) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 501(5) The penalty for the offences in subsections (3) and (4) (src:7085-7085)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 501(5) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3) or (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a liability only "on summary conviction"
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 501(6)
-- Plain gloss: nothing in s 501 takes away the auditor's right to apply for an injunction (in Scotland an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce his rights under s 499 or 500.
-- src:7086 | (6) Nothing in this section affects any right of an auditor to apply for an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce any of his rights under section 499 or 500.
@ref s 501(6) The auditor's right to apply for an injunction is not affected (src:7086-7086)
GIVEN `the right is the auditor's right to apply for an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce any of his rights under section 499 or 500` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(6) the section affects the auditor's right to apply for an injunction` MEANS
    IF `the right is the auditor's right to apply for an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce any of his rights under section 499 or 500`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects any right of an auditor to apply for an injunction ... to enforce any of his rights under section 499 or 500"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of that right

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 502  Auditor's rights in relation to resolutions and meetings
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 502(1)
-- Plain gloss: for a private company's written resolution, the auditor is entitled to get everything a member is entitled to be sent under Chapter 2 of Part 13.
-- src:7088 | (1) In relation to a written resolution proposed to be agreed to by a private company, the company's auditor is entitled to receive all such communications relating to the resolution as, by virtue of any provision of Chapter 2 of Part 13 of this Act, are required to be supplied to a member of the company.
@ref s 502(1) Written resolutions of a private company (src:7088-7088)
GIVEN `s 288 the resolution is a written resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is one that, by virtue of a provision of Chapter 2 of Part 13, is required to be supplied to a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502(1) the auditor is entitled to receive the communication` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 288 the resolution is a written resolution`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND `the communication is one that, by virtue of a provision of Chapter 2 of Part 13, is required to be supplied to a member of the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a written resolution proposed to be agreed to by a private company, the company's auditor is entitled to receive all such communications ... as ... are required to be supplied to a member"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is "In relation to a written resolution"; the subsection does not speak of other resolutions
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resolution is a written resolution is section 288 (coa7), not known

-- COVERS: s 502(2)(a)
-- Plain gloss: the auditor is entitled to get every notice and communication about a general meeting that a member is entitled to get.
-- src:7089 | (2) A company's auditor is entitled—
-- src:7090 | (a) to receive all notices of, and other communications relating to, any general meeting which a member of the company is entitled to receive,
@ref s 502(2)(a) Notices of general meetings (src:7089-7090)
GIVEN `the notice or communication relates to a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member of the company is entitled to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502(2)(a) the auditor is entitled to receive the notice or communication` MEANS
    IF `the notice or communication relates to a general meeting of the company` AND `a member of the company is entitled to receive it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to receive all notices of, and other communications relating to, any general meeting which a member of the company is entitled to receive"

-- COVERS: s 502(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the auditor is entitled to attend any general meeting.
-- src:7089 | (2) A company's auditor is entitled—
-- src:7091 | (b) to attend any general meeting of the company, and
@ref s 502(2)(b) Attending general meetings (src:7089-7091)
