-- COVERS: s 506(2), s 506(2)(a), s 506(2)(b), s 506(2)(b)(i), s 506(2)(b)(ii), s 506(2)(b)(iii)
-- Plain gloss: the conditions: the company, thinking on reasonable grounds that naming the auditor would create a serious risk of violence or intimidation, has resolved not to state the name, and has told the Secretary of State of the resolution, giving the company's name and number, the financial year, and the names of the auditor and (for a firm) the senior statutory auditor.
-- src:7124 | (2) The conditions are that the company—
-- src:7125 | (a) considering on reasonable grounds that statement of the name would create or be likely to create a serious risk that the auditor or senior statutory auditor, or any other person, would be subject to violence or intimidation, has resolved that the name should not be stated, and
-- src:7126 | (b) has given notice of the resolution to the Secretary of State, stating—
-- src:7127 | (i) the name and registered number of the company,
-- src:7128 | (ii) the financial year of the company to which the report relates, and
-- src:7129 | (iii) the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed the report as senior statutory auditor.
@ref s 506(2) The conditions (src:7124-7129)
GIVEN `the company considers on reasonable grounds that stating the name would create or be likely to create a serious risk that the auditor or senior statutory auditor, or any other person, would be subject to violence or intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has resolved that the name should not be stated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has given notice of the resolution to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the name and registered number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the financial year of the company to which the report relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed the report as senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 506(2) the conditions for omitting the names are met` MEANS
    IF       `the company considers on reasonable grounds that stating the name would create or be likely to create a serious risk that the auditor or senior statutory auditor, or any other person, would be subject to violence or intimidation`
         AND `the company has resolved that the name should not be stated`
         AND `the company has given notice of the resolution to the Secretary of State`
         AND `the notice states the name and registered number of the company`
         AND `the notice states the financial year of the company to which the report relates`
         AND `the notice states the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed the report as senior statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that the company— (a) considering on reasonable grounds ..., has resolved ..., and (b) has given notice of the resolution to the Secretary of State, stating— (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) ..."

-- s 506(1): which copies the names may be left out of.
DECLARE `s 506(1) kind of copy of the report` IS ONE OF
    `s 506(1)(a) a published copy of the report`
    `s 506(1)(b) the copy delivered to the registrar under Chapter 10 of Part 15`
    `s 506(1) another copy`

