        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person to whom this section applies commits an offence if he knowingly or recklessly causes such a report to omit a statement required by— (a) section 498(2)(b) ..., (b) section 498(3) ..., or (c) section 498(5)" (an offence defined by "if": marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 507(4), s 507(4)(a), s 507(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine up to the statutory maximum. No imprisonment.
-- src:7140 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:7141 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:7142 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 507(4) The penalty (src:7140-7142)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 507(4) the penalty for an offence under section 507` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- ss 508 and 509  Guidance for regulatory and prosecuting authorities
-- (these provisions address only officials; layer 1 records what they decide, and layer 2 has no question for them)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 508(1), s 508(1)(a), s 508(1)(b), s 508(1)(b)(i), s 508(1)(b)(ii), s 508(2), s 508(4)
-- Plain gloss: the Secretary of State may issue guidance to help regulators and prosecutors on behaviour that appears to be an s 507 offence and is or may be under investigation; he must first obtain the Attorney General's consent; the section does not apply to Scotland.
-- src:7144 | (1) The Secretary of State may issue guidance for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities to determine how they should carry out their functions in cases where behaviour occurs that—
-- src:7145 | (a) appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507 (offences in connection with auditor's report), and
-- src:7146 | (b) has been, is being or may be investigated—
-- src:7147 | (i) pursuant to arrangements under paragraph 15 of Schedule 10 (investigation of complaints against auditors and supervisory bodies), or
-- src:7148 | (ii) by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
-- src:7149 | (2) The Secretary of State must obtain the consent of the Attorney General before issuing any such guidance.
-- src:7156 | (4) This section does not apply to Scotland.
@ref s 508(1)-(2), (4) The Secretary of State's guidance (src:7144-7156)
GIVEN `the guidance is for Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance is for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities to determine how they should carry out their functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the behaviour appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the behaviour has been, is being or may be investigated pursuant to arrangements under paragraph 15 of Schedule 10, or by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has obtained the consent of the Attorney General before issuing the guidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508(1) the Secretary of State may issue the guidance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the guidance is for Scotland` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to Scotland."
        IF NOT (    `the guidance is for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities to determine how they should carry out their functions`
                AND `the behaviour appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507`
                AND `the behaviour has been, is being or may be investigated pursuant to arrangements under paragraph 15 of Schedule 10, or by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may issue guidance for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities ... in cases where behaviour occurs that— (a) appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507 ..., and (b) has been, is being or may be investigated"
        IF (NOT `the Secretary of State has obtained the consent of the Attorney General before issuing the guidance`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must obtain the consent of the Attorney General before issuing any such guidance" (fork F2: a bare "must" not done)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 508(3), s 508(3)(a), s 508(3)(b), s 508(3)(c), s 508(3)(d), s 508(3)(e)
-- Plain gloss: the "relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities" are supervisory bodies under Part 42, the bodies the Secretary of State may fund under s 16(1) of the 2004 Act, the Director of the SFO, the DPP (or DPP for Northern Ireland), and the Secretary of State.
-- src:7150 | (3) In this section “relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities” means—
-- src:7151 | (a) supervisory bodies within the meaning of Part 42 of this Act,
-- src:7152 | (b) bodies to which the Secretary of State may make grants under section 16(1) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27) (bodies concerned with accounting standards etc),
-- src:7153 | (c) the Director of the Serious Fraud Office,
-- src:7154 | (d) the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland, and
-- src:7155 | (e) the Secretary of State.
@ref s 508(3) "relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities" (src:7150-7155)
GIVEN `the body is a supervisory body within the meaning of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is one to which the Secretary of State may make grants under section 16(1) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Director of the Serious Fraud Office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508(3) the body is one of the relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities` MEANS
    IF `the body is a supervisory body within the meaning of Part 42` OR `the body is one to which the Secretary of State may make grants under section 16(1) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` OR `the person is the Director of the Serious Fraud Office` OR `the person is the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` OR `the person is the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant regulatory and prosecuting authorities” means— (a) ... (e) the Secretary of State"

-- COVERS: s 509(1), s 509(1)(a), s 509(1)(b), s 509(1)(b)(i), s 509(1)(b)(ii), s 509(2), s 509(4)
-- Plain gloss: the Lord Advocate may issue the same kind of guidance for Scotland, after consulting the Secretary of State; the section applies only to Scotland.
-- src:7158 | (1) The Lord Advocate may issue guidance for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory authorities to determine how they should carry out their functions in cases where behaviour occurs that—
-- src:7159 | (a) appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507 (offences in connection with auditor's report), and
-- src:7160 | (b) has been, is being or may be investigated—
-- src:7161 | (i) pursuant to arrangements under paragraph 15 of Schedule 10 (investigation of complaints against auditors and supervisory bodies), or
-- src:7162 | (ii) by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
-- src:7163 | (2) The Lord Advocate must consult the Secretary of State before issuing any such guidance.
-- src:7168 | (4) This section applies only to Scotland.
@ref s 509(1)-(2), (4) The Lord Advocate's guidance (src:7158-7168)
GIVEN `the guidance is for Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance is for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory authorities to determine how they should carry out their functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the behaviour appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the behaviour has been, is being or may be investigated pursuant to arrangements under paragraph 15 of Schedule 10, or by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Lord Advocate has consulted the Secretary of State before issuing the guidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 509(1) the Lord Advocate may issue the guidance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the guidance is for Scotland`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only to Scotland."
        IF NOT (    `the guidance is for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory authorities to determine how they should carry out their functions`
                AND `the behaviour appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507`
                AND `the behaviour has been, is being or may be investigated pursuant to arrangements under paragraph 15 of Schedule 10, or by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may issue guidance for the purpose of helping relevant regulatory authorities ... in cases where behaviour occurs that— (a) appears to involve the commission of an offence under section 507 ..., and (b) has been, is being or may be investigated"
        IF (NOT `the Lord Advocate has consulted the Secretary of State before issuing the guidance`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Lord Advocate must consult the Secretary of State before issuing any such guidance" (fork F2: a bare "must" not done)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 509(3), s 509(3)(a), s 509(3)(b), s 509(3)(c)
-- Plain gloss: the "relevant regulatory authorities" are supervisory bodies under Part 42, the bodies the Secretary of State may fund under s 16(1) of the 2004 Act, and the Secretary of State.
-- src:7164 | (3) In this section “relevant regulatory authorities” means—
-- src:7165 | (a) supervisory bodies within the meaning of Part 42 of this Act,
-- src:7166 | (b) bodies to which the Secretary of State may make grants under section 16(1) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27) (bodies concerned with accounting standards etc), and
-- src:7167 | (c) the Secretary of State.
@ref s 509(3) "relevant regulatory authorities" (src:7164-7167)
GIVEN `the body is a supervisory body within the meaning of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is one to which the Secretary of State may make grants under section 16(1) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 509(3) the body is one of the relevant regulatory authorities` MEANS
    IF `the body is a supervisory body within the meaning of Part 42` OR `the body is one to which the Secretary of State may make grants under section 16(1) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` OR `the person is the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant regulatory authorities” means— (a) ... (b) ..., and (c) the Secretary of State"
